# W17.3 cel-spec corpus integrity manifest (VAL-W17-010).
#
# sha256sum-compatible format. Each non-comment line is:
#     <64 lowercase hex digits><two spaces><relative path>
#
# Verify locally with:
#     cd tests/conformance/cel-spec && sha256sum -c MANIFEST.sha256
# (or `shasum -a 256 -c` on macOS).
#
# PINNED_COMMIT.txt and MANIFEST.sha256 itself are deliberately
# excluded -- PINNED_COMMIT.txt is the upstream-anchor (validated by
# the nightly drift workflow's git ls-remote check) and MANIFEST.sha256
# cannot contain its own digest.
#
# Updating any covered file REQUIRES regenerating this manifest. The
# drift checker (scripts/check-cel-spec-drift.py) AND the per-file
# digest test in test_w17_3_celspec_corpus.py both flag mismatches.

03a3414f85a1e5cc176c161d091dcc304a303d0cc79e5ae64c13617e2391cc68  .upstream-pins.json
56fceed52363d5a6780ced0ec31eeba02032710d222894c1c8ce83a54958664f  celspec_vectors.json
4fb0a928d8667355a55c24e12327b2ff53a79454bccbb29164a3b1cdd7417046  relay-profile-filter.yaml
